Go build/vet/test workflow on push+PR, matrix go.mod-minimum 1.22.x + stable, verified locally at e060e2e

## Why
mpbt-hq/starfleetctl had no build/test CI: the only workflow was the Dependabot "Dependency Graph" (`dynamic/dependabot/update-graph`). Measured consequences at every review head: check-runs total_count 0, combined status total_count 0, no PR — i.e. exact-head CI was not producible at all (infrastructure gap, not a red run). This is W0-134 blocker (c).

## Change
Branch `wt/ci-build-test`, commit f7065b6b44b2a8dbbe0354154ff24c6e515fcf5f, based on origin/master e060e2eed70817e78c3686d0a4960e1d180f7336. One new file: `.github/workflows/build-test.yml` (34 lines, SPDX AGPL-3.0-or-later, tooling license per workspace policy).

- triggers: every push (all branches) and every pull_request → any review branch (e.g. work/wormhole-manager-w0-017) gets an exact-head check-runs result
- runner: ubuntu-latest; Go matrix: "1.22.x" (the minimum declared in go.mod) + "stable", fail-fast: false
- steps: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1 -timeout 300s`
- concurrency group per ref with cancel-in-progress
- deliberately NOT `make all`: that target includes check-plugin, which needs node/esbuild and is not available on a bare runner

## Local verification (worktree wt/ci-build-test at e060e2e)
- YAML parses (python yaml.safe_load): jobs=[build-test], matrix=[1.22.x, stable], on=[push, pull_request]
- the workflow steps were executed verbatim:
  - go build ./... → EXIT=0
  - go vet ./... → EXIT=0
  - go test ./... -count=1 -timeout 300s → all packages ok except internal/session:
    - FAIL: TestRunClientEnvShipTarget — "STARFLEET_TARGET should not be set for role=flagship: STARFLEET_TARGET=Enterprise"
    - root cause measured: the test reads the env built by runClientEnv, which inherits the process environment. It PASSES with a clean environment (`env -u STARFLEET_TARGET -u STARFLEET_SHIP_ID go test ./internal/session/ -run TestRunClientEnvShipTarget -count=1` → PASS) and FAILS only inside a ship shell where STARFLEET_TARGET=Enterprise / STARFLEET_SHIP_ID=LaForge are exported. Hosted GitHub runners have neither variable → CI is green. The test is env-sensitive, not broken.
    - internal/wormhole: ok 167.856s (89 sequential git-integration tests) → the 300s timeout is justified; a tighter one flakes
- go.mod minimum: `GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.22.12 go build ./...` → EXIT=0 (toolchain downloaded, build clean) → the "1.22.x" matrix leg is safe
- Logs: `_WORK_/starfleetctl/tmp/logs-ci-branch/full-suite.log`, `go122-build.log`

